   <NOTE uuid="{6f9812e6-bc18-4792-af9a-5980af5be18b}">
    <X>257</X>
    <Y>40</Y>
    <Z>40000</Z>
    <TEXT translate="true">1. Switch to Similation mode

2. Do dhcp request from PC0

3. DHCP Request fails and PC0 gets an APIPA address which is 169.254.213.152
(AND product of 169.254.0.0 &amp;&amp; the last 2 bytes of the port Mac Address)

4. Gratuitous Arp is sent out from PC0 to check for duplicate address.

5. From PC1, request DHCP and expect PC1 to also get the address 169.254.213.152
( since the last 2 bytes of the port mac address is the same as in PC0)

6. PC1 sends out Gratuious ARP and gets a reply.

7. PC1 now gets a new APIPA address 169.254.213.153

8. PC1 sends out another Gratuitous ARP and no reply so it keeps the address.</TEXT>
    <NOTECLUSTERID>1-1</NOTECLUSTERID>
